Since `TimeProvider` is in DI but static classes can't receive constructor injection, you have two options:

**Option 1 (Recommended): Convert to a non-static class**

```csharp
public class TimestampFormatter
{
    private readonly TimeProvider _timeProvider;

    public TimestampFormatter(TimeProvider timeProvider)
    {
        _timeProvider = timeProvider;
    }

    public string Format() => _timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("o");
}
```

Register it: `services.AddSingleton<TimestampFormatter>();`

**Option 2: Keep static, accept TimeProvider as a parameter**

```csharp
public static class TimestampFormatter
{
    public static string Format(TimeProvider timeProvider)
        => timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("o");
}
```

---

**Option 1 is preferred** because it keeps call sites clean, is naturally testable (inject `FakeTimeProvider` in tests), and follows the same DI pattern as the rest of your app.

